# What must never be uploaded to a build.
#
# `vercel deploy` reads THIS file, not .gitignore. Without it the CLI uploads
# everything, .env included — and Next fills any variable Vercel does not set
# from that file. Two live symptoms came from exactly that: production reaching
# for a database at 127.0.0.1 (this machine's DATABASE_URL) and accepting a
# webhook signed with a local test secret.
#
# Real configuration belongs in Vercel's own environment variables, where it is
# scoped per environment and never travels in a source upload.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local state and build output the remote build has no use for.
.next
node_modules
.vercel
lib/generated
.tmp
.tmp-audit

# Machine-specific tooling.
.claude/skills
